WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
A balloon inflates beside a ruler.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:07.360
Every second, its radius grows
by exactly one centimetre.

3
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.390
But watch the volume counter.

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.300
Each second, it jumps by more
than it did the second before.

5
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.050
The radius is steady.

6
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.790
So why does the volume grow ever faster?

7
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.220
Is the air being pumped in faster?

8
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.650
In this mission, you'll link
two rates through a formula:

9
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.540
the volume of a sphere, V
equals four thirds pi r cubed.

10
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:33.690
You'll use the chain rule to
connect d V by d t with d r by d t.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.260
And you'll warm up on a ripple in a pond,

12
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:42.030
its area pi r squared, its radius
spreading at two centimetres per second.

13
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.370
Your mission: explain why the
balloon's volume grows ever faster.
